/data/vm/vm-bake
# @summary vm-bake's own dataset and directory: the datasets image/ (the sealed images), guest/ (the clones) and data/ (the data disks of the guests: zvols that outlive their guests, template data add), and the directory distfiles/ for what comes from outside, by kind: image/ (VM images), pkg/ (package files), later deb/, rpm/, port/. Made once by root and delegated to the invoking user: zfs create <pool>/.../vm-bake, chown <user> on its mount point, zfs allow <user> create,mount,snapshot,clone,destroy,readonly,volsize,userprop on it, sysctl vfs.usermount=1 -- then every ZFS act of vm-bake runs without root. vm-bhyve keeps its own directory (VM_BAKE_VM_DIR).
